gnu-apl (2.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Patch ⎕RVAL to build random floats independently of byte order;
    fixes garbage random numbers on big-endian architectures
  * Patch configure to compute the socket constants of FIO∆SockHelper
    (wslib5/FILE_IO.apl) from the target's headers instead of shipping
    x86 values, wrong on alpha, hppa, mips and sparc; and File_IO.tc and
    Quad_FIO.tc to use them instead of hard-coding SOL_SOCKET etc.; the
    test run hung there
  * Patch configure to expand ${prefix} in --libdir, and take the
    LIBREF-3/4/5 library paths in /etc/gnu-apl.d/preferences from
    libdir; fixes )LOAD 5 FILE_IO and friends, broken by the multiarch
    libdir
  * Patch ⎕FIO ¯8/¯9 (screen size) to not return garbage when stdin is
    not a terminal
  * Fix Quad_ES.tc expected output, broken by the spelling patch
  * Take fixes of MultiLineLiterals.tc and ZZ59_Regression.tc from
    upstream trunk
  * autopkgtest: set up the environment of upstream's make test (--id
    1010, $HOME, library 0 with ASSERT.apl), allowing most previously
    skipped testcases to run

 -- Barak A. Pearlmutter <bap@debian.org>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 15:23:39 +0000

gnu-apl (2.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Patch to stop configuring upstream debian/ subdirectory
  * Remove unused patch 0003-deconstruct-info-to-texi.patch
  * Drop superfluous debian/copyright stanzas for removed m4 files
  * Rewrite "#!/usr/bin/env -S apl" shebangs to /usr/bin/apl
  * Patch to not redefine libstdc++ _Atomic_word, fixes sparc64 FTBFS
  * Bump to debhelper compat level 14
  * Add autopkgtests: smoke test, and upstream src/testcases (each run
    in a fresh interpreter, skipping those that fail in 2.0)
  * Cherry-pick upstream fix for QR factorization (⌹[⎕CT]B) segfault,
    and enable MatrixInverse.tc in autopkgtest
  * Patch CDR decoding (11/12 ⎕CR, ⎕TF, shared variables, AP210) to use
    the little-endian byte order it is encoded in; fixes corruption on
    big-endian architectures, and of nested Unicode scalars everywhere
  * Patch packed Boolean ravels: host-independent byte order, fix
    )SAVE/)LOAD of packed values (garbage on all architectures), and 41
    ⎕CR
  * autopkgtest: skip two testcases whose expected output assumes x87
    80-bit long double, except on amd64 and i386

 -- Barak A. Pearlmutter <bap@debian.org>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 13:38:12 +0000

